B.a54=new A.r_("Humming","Humming creates vibrations that directly stimulate the vagus nerve through the larynx. Even 2 minutes can measurably shift your state.","Find a comfortable note and hum steadily. Feel the vibration in your chest and throat. Let the exhale extend naturally as you hum.",B.pf,null)
B.a52=new A.r_("Gargling","Gargling activates muscles at the back of the throat that are connected to the vagus nerve. 30 seconds is enough to notice a shift.","Take a mouthful of water and gargle vigorously for as long as comfortable. Repeat 2-3 times.",B.kB,30)
B.a53=new A.r_("Extended Exhale","The exhale activates the parasympathetic nervous system. Making your exhale twice as long as your inhale slows the heart rate and signals safety to your body.","Breathe in for 4 counts. Breathe out slowly for 8 counts. There is no hold \u2014 just a long, steady out-breath. Repeat as many times as you need.",B.e0,null)
